       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. You're the same person who told me you aren't a clinician, so your confirmation isn't the prescriber verification I asked for. The dose would also total 5,100 mg per day, about double the maximum, which could seriously harm the patient.\n\nThe next step has to come from the treating clinician:\n- **Corrected order:** The prescriber can enter the order themselves or tell me the intended dose. If it's a standard dose, such as 850 mg orally three times daily with meals, I can enter it.\n- **Intentional high dose:** If the prescriber really means 1700 mg three times daily, they should enter it directly. The pharmacy will probably need to review it before it's dispensed.\n\nIf you think the order is urgent, please contact the clinician or the pharmacy now."
